;; sandbox_check.sb — Seatbelt profile TEMPLATE for the S2-Lean checker (repair round 1, D4 step 2 / refuter R1).
;; check.py renders __LEAN_BIN__ and __WRITE_PATHS__ and passes the text to `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec -p`, around
;; every `lean` it runs on agent-influenced text (the canonical compile) and, for uniformity, around the pristine
;; compile and the s2audit run. Seatbelt is LAST-MATCH-WINS: the allows must come AFTER the denies.
;;
;; What it fences:
;;   network*        — no sockets of any kind (an in-body `#eval IO.Process.run curl …` cannot reach the net)
;;   process-fork    — lean may not create ANY child process: `IO.Process.spawn/output/run` fail with
;;                     "operation not permitted", so no background writer can outlive the compile and no
;;                     shell runs as the Studio user at check time (refuter R1's `id` / curl / writeFile chain)
;;   process-exec*   — only the pinned toolchain `lean` binary may be exec'd (sandbox-exec's own exec of it)
;;   file-write*     — denied everywhere EXCEPT the fresh per-check work dir rendered below (cwork, the ONLY
;;                     writable path — never $ST/$BENCH, so a body cannot overwrite bodies.json: AP-1) and
;;                     /dev/null. TMPDIR is set to cwork so lean's scratch stays inside.
;;   file-read*      — DENIED for the credential/config trees (__DENY_READ__: ~/.claude-bench, ~/.claude, ~/.ssh,
;;                     ~/.aws, keychains, …) so an `include_str`/#eval cannot read a secret into log_tail (AP-2);
;;                     otherwise reads are allowed (Lean must read ~2 GB of Mathlib oleans). The stage-A olean is
;;                     copied INTO cwork so the audit reads nothing under $BENCH/state.
;;
;; Why `lean` directly and not `lake env lean`: the exec allow-list admits ONE binary; `lake` would have to be
;; allowed too, and lake forks lean. check.py takes LEAN_PATH/PATH from `lake env env` (harness-side, no agent
;; text) and runs the toolchain lean under this profile. `lake env lean -o` itself was verified to need NO
;; writes into the project (.lake is write-denied here and the compile succeeds).
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network*)
(deny process-fork)
(deny process-exec*)
__DENY_READ__
(allow process-exec (literal "__LEAN_BIN__"))
(deny file-write*)
(allow file-write* __WRITE_PATHS__ (literal "/dev/null"))
